        idea: "Every metre is a sequence of light (laghu) and heavy (guru) syllables, so all possible metres of n syllables can be listed systematically — 2ⁿ patterns.",
        more: "Pingala’s Chandahshastra (Pingala Sutras) is the earliest known treatise on Sanskrit prosody and one of the six Vedangas (chhandas). Its rules for counting metres amount to a binary number system and the combinatorics later seen in Pascal’s triangle (Meru-prastara, named by commentator Halayudha in the 10th c.) and Fibonacci-type sequences (later formalised by Virahanka and Hemachandra). It also uses shunya as a marker.",
